# D0.7.2 universal public parity & conversion acceptance protocol

**Test definitions and synthetic fixture expectations only; NOT RUN.** Use isolated synthetic participants, no real credentials, live purchases or private account content. `D072_PUBLIC_PARITY.json` contains two equivalent inputs varying only acquisition code. Replay both through the same installed candidate and deterministic test instrument; compare CFM4 results, first response coverage, Free entitlement and same published offer card. Do NOT claim identical model prose is required—compare substantive facts and access/routing. No automatic Premium, church affiliation, recipient sharing or ForgedLife enrollment. Test sign-in and recovery as an application integration run, not by simulated controller alone.

`D072_CONVERSION_COHORT.json` supplies synthetic timestamps, click/checkout-only decoys, within-window confirmed Premium, after-window confirmed Premium, Full-only purchase, duplicate webhook and refund. Run a deterministic cohort calculation with UTC exclusive boundaries and unique participant denominator. Missing consent/source must not lead to unauthorized joins. Validate events do not carry personal content. Unmatured cohorts must be labeled partial, not final. `D072_RELEASE_GATE.json` ensures a proposed broad-public flag cannot override the inherited pilot restriction without actual release authorization.

Each run requires immutable fixture SHA, application build and prompt/source hashes, API traces with sanitized identifiers, scorer version, event/consent source, actual executed assertions and per-criterion PASS/FAIL/NOT RUN; human reviewers separately evaluate teaching depth, relevance and appropriate challenge. Existing D0.7.1 / historical tests are not automatically credited by these new fixtures.
